  "notes": "Generated from a published construction, not transcribed and not new. (a, b) is a Golay pair of length 10; with p = (a+b)/2 and m = (a-b)/2, Turyn's product X = a x p + rev(b) x m, Y = b x p - rev(a) x m is a Golay pair of length 100. A, B, C, D = X, Y, [1], [1] are base sequences of lengths 100, 100, 1, 1, and T_1 = (A+B)/2;0, T_2 = (A-B)/2;0, T_3 = 0;1, T_4 = 0 are T-sequences of length 101. The rows are T_1+T_2+T_3+T_4, -T_1+T_2+T_3-T_4, -T_1-T_2+T_3+T_4 and -T_1+T_2-T_3+T_4, whose Goethals-Seidel array is the Cooper-Wallis Hadamard matrix of order 404. The script in the evidence file checks the Golay identities at lengths 10 and 100, the base-sequence identity, the T-sequence support and identity, and the PAF identity of the rows. The board had no quadruple at n = 101 before."
